# A1-P02 — The Wrong Weapon. Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1221–1311.
# Scene: scenes/chapter1/elara_meeting.tscn. The combat tutorial happens only
# when danger can't be avoided: the slime follows if you back off and attacks
# if you wait.
# Every branch keeps Elara with Kaelen. The legacy flags ch1_elara_trusted and
# ch1_elara_cautious are what GameManager.has_elara() reads.
# rhythm: clipped after_slime
# (Elara's questioning at bow-point is meant to be terse: name, origin, facts.)

~ start
Kaelen: Hang on. Why is there a sword on my belt?
Kaelen: I don't own a sword. I've never owned a sword in my life.
Kaelen: ...Apparently I own a sword.
do slime_appears

~ after_slime
Kaelen: That wasn't blood. That wasn't anything. It just... came apart.
???: Were you hoping it would be blood?
do elara_enters
Elara: Hands where I can see them.
Kaelen: One of them's holding a sword. Sorry. That's new.
Elara: Then put that one down first.
Kaelen: Okay. Putting it down. Slowly. Nobody panic.
do kaelen_lowers_sword
Elara: Name?
Kaelen: Kaelen.
Elara: From where?
Kaelen: Flight 707.
Elara: Is that a place?
Kaelen: It's a plane. It— it flies. It's a big metal thing full of people, and it flies.
# She looks at him the way you'd look at someone describing a dragon made of spoons.
Kaelen: You didn't see anything fall today? Out of the sky, near here?
Elara: You.
Kaelen: Anyone else? Smoke, wreckage, people walking around in shock?
Elara: No. Nothing like that.
Elara: Were there supposed to be?
Kaelen: ...A lot of them.
do elara_lowers_bow
Elara: Then let's talk somewhere the road isn't trying to eat us.
? Kaelen (Internal): How much do I tell her?
- I was on a flight. Something happened, I woke up here, and everyone else is gone. => trust
- There were people with me. I need to find them before I explain the rest. => cautious
- You first. Where am I? Then I'll tell you how impossible this is. => deflect

~ trust
set elara_first_truth
set ch1_elara_trusted
do trust elara 10
Elara: You remember them. Their faces, I mean, not just that they were there.
Kaelen: Enough of them. Some.
Elara: Good. Hold on to that as hard as you can.
Kaelen: Why is that good?
Elara: Because the people who walk out of bad places usually walk out remembering less.
=> after

~ cautious
set elara_first_cautious
set ch1_elara_cautious
Elara: You remember enough to be careful. That's something.
Kaelen: I remember enough to know I should be looking for them, not standing here.
Elara: Then we want the same thing, for now. Somewhere with walls first.
=> after

~ deflect
set elara_first_deflect
set ch1_elara_cautious
Elara: You're in Oakhaven Reach.
Kaelen: Is that a country?
Elara: A region. The country's a long argument; nobody agrees where it starts.
Kaelen: Fine. Which world, then? Where is all of this?
Elara: Aethelgard.
Kaelen (Internal): Nothing. It's not a word I know. It's not even close to one.
=> after

~ after
set elara_met
Elara: You came out of the crater, stranger.
Kaelen: I suppose I did. I woke up in it, anyway.
Elara: People don't come out of the crater.
Kaelen: Great. Today's going great. Really.
Elara: Oakhaven keeps road records. Travellers, strangers... things that fall out of places they shouldn't.
Kaelen: That happens often enough that someone writes it down?
Elara: Often enough that Bran complains about the paperwork every single time.
do kaelen_reaches_for_sword
do elara_raises_bow
Kaelen: Right. Sorry. I'll leave that where it is.
Elara: Walk ahead of me, where I can see you.
Kaelen: Very trusting of you.
Elara: Very practical. You'd do the same.
do objective Reach Oakhaven. Follow the first lead on the missing passengers.
